a huge controversy has wracked the cs go  community  the decision by face it admins running  flashpoint season 3  to replay a game that had already been  completed  for some it was an example of a big org  flexing their muscle  to get the outcome they wanted for  others it was a disaster from the get-go  and potentially  mishandled by the face at admins running  flashpoint  but wherever you land on this issue one  thing is clear  the cs go community isn't happy and  they shouldn't be  listen i'm sure a lot of people involved  in this situation regret their tweets  life choices maybe even more but you  know what you won't regret  subscribing to the score esports youtube  channel  hit that subscribe button ring the  notification bell  leave me a comment about how i  apparently look like maggie  gyllenhaal and that way when we have  fresh  content available you'll see it right  away  okay so let's start at the beginning on  friday may 14th  ninjas in pajamas faced anonymous  esports a polish esports organization  as part of flashpoint season 3. in case  you missed the recent news the series  was also the debut of device  the ex-astralis superstar that ninjas  and pajamas added to their already  impressive roster  don't get me wrong mechanically simple  is the de facto filthiest fragger ever  to touch cs go with  zywoo hot on his trail but in terms of  results  accolades and well pretty much every  other metric you can imagine  device takes the cake it's not even  close it's fair to say that a lot of  people  expected nip to win but when the time  came for the match to get underway on  friday  there was a long technical pause due to  a complaint from nip that  they were experiencing severe lag due in  part at least  to packet loss to really oversimplify  this  packet loss happens when some of the  data saved between  a player's go client and a server just  never arrives what this could look like  is your enemy's positions may not update  accurately on your end your posi